From: RTSP-on-GE11 contributors <noreply@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] mfmediaengine: preserve a newly selected frame's tick result

A3.20: integrated after GE-Proton11-6 and the project seek/error patches.
Historical A3.19 inputs and installed artifacts remain unchanged.

GE's ge-video-rework/0015 changed sample_get_pts() to expose future PTS and
assigned its result to the enclosing loop's hr. A due frame followed by a
future frame therefore selects the due presentation sample but reports
S_FALSE and the future PTS to OnVideoStreamTick(). Discarding a trailing
preroll sample can likewise overwrite a successful selection with S_FALSE.

Preserve S_OK and the PTS of a frame selected during this call, unless a
later sample produces an actual failure. Do not report an old presentation
sample just because preroll was discarded. Keep future-only results,
preroll filtering, errors, queue mutations and sample requests unchanged.

This corrects the function's explicit selected-frame contract. Its cause
and effect are source-demonstrable; association with WaterWolf choppiness or
episode #331 seek stalls is NOT established. A subsequent tick can already
recover an unpresented frame, so this is not proof of a permanent stall.
The accompanying Python model is not execution of Wine C or a playback test.

The license of the modified Wine source file applies to this patch.
---
diff --git a/dlls/mfmediaengine/video_frame_sink.c b/dlls/mfmediaengine/video_frame_sink.c
--- a/dlls/mfmediaengine/video_frame_sink.c
+++ b/dlls/mfmediaengine/video_frame_sink.c
@@ -1315,7 +1315,7 @@ HRESULT video_frame_sink_get_pts_after(struct video_frame_sink *sink, MFTIME clocktime, LONGLONG min_pts,
     if (sink)
     {
         IMFSample *sample;
-        bool transfer_sample = FALSE;
+        bool transfer_sample = FALSE, selected_sample = FALSE;
         BOOL preroll_sample;
         EnterCriticalSection(&sink->cs);
         while (video_frame_sink_sample_queue_pop(sink, &sample))
@@ -1325,6 +1325,8 @@ HRESULT video_frame_sink_get_pts_after(struct video_frame_sink *sink, MFTIME clocktime, LONGLONG min_pts,
             {
                 video_frame_sink_sample_queue_set_presentation(sink, sample);
                 transfer_sample = TRUE;
+                selected_sample = TRUE;
+                sample_pts = *pts;
             }
             else if (preroll_sample)
             {
@@ -1348,6 +1350,13 @@ HRESULT video_frame_sink_get_pts_after(struct video_frame_sink *sink, MFTIME clocktime, LONGLONG min_pts,
                 *pts = sample_pts;
         }
 
+        /* A future or preroll sample must not hide a frame selected above. */
+        if (selected_sample && SUCCEEDED(hr))
+        {
+            hr = S_OK;
+            *pts = sample_pts;
+        }
+
         LeaveCriticalSection(&sink->cs);
     }
 
